<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/suket-satyagraha"><span class="enc-name">Suket Satyagraha</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Suket Satyagraha was a popular movement in the princely state of Suket, in the hills of present-day Himachal Pradesh, in February 1948.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sukhra"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sukhra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sukhra</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sukhra, also called Zarmihr, was a Sasanian nobleman of the House of Karen who dominated the Iranian court in the 480s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sukkal"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sukkal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sukkal</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">Sukkal was a title of high office in ancient Elam, originally meaning envoy or minister.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sukkalmah"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sukkalmah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sukkalmah</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">Sukkalmah, meaning grand regent, was the title of the supreme ruler of Elam during the Sukkalmah period.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sukkalmah-period"><span class="enc-name">Sukkalmah period</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sukkalmah period was the era of Elamite history c. 1970–1500 BCE, when Elam was ruled by grand regents called sukkalmahs.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sukkur"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sukkur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sukkur</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sukkur is a city on the right bank of the Indus in Sindh province, Pakistan, opposite Rohri.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sula-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sula-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sula (river)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sula is a river of north-eastern Ukraine, about 360 km long, a left tributary of the Dnieper.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sulaiman-badrul-alam-shah"><span class="enc-name">Sulaiman Badrul Alam Shah</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sulaiman Badrul Alam Shah was sultan of Johor and Riau from 1722 to 1760.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sulaimanu-of-kano"><span class="enc-name">Sulaimanu of Kano</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sulaimanu was the first Fulani emir of Kano in northern Nigeria, ruling from 1807 to 1819.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sulawesi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sulawesi</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sulawesi is a large island in eastern Indonesia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sulayhid-dynasty"><span class="enc-name">Sulayhid dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sulayhid dynasty was an Isma'ili Shia dynasty that ruled much of Yemen from about 1047 to 1138 as allies of the Fatimid caliphs of Cairo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sulayman-abu-layla-pasha"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sulayman-abu-layla-pasha.jpg" alt="" loading="l