ia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-bin-muhammad-al-qasimi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sultan-bin-muhammad-al-qasimi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sultan bin Muhammad Al Qasimi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan bin Muhammad Al Qasimi has been ruler of Sharjah, one of the United Arab Emirates, since 1972, when he succeeded his brother Khalid after a failed coup.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-bin-saqr-al-qasimi"><span class="enc-name">Sultan bin Saqr Al Qasimi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan bin Saqr Al Qasimi was sheikh of the Qawasim of Ras al-Khaimah and Sharjah for most of the period from 1803 to 1866.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-hadlirin"><span class="enc-name">Sultan Hadlirin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan Hadlirin was ruler of Kalinyamat near Jepara on the north coast of Java and husband of a daughter of Sultan Trenggana of Demak.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-hasanuddin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sultan-hasanuddin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sultan Hasanuddin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan Hasanuddin was the sixteenth ruler of the Makassarese kingdom of Gowa in South Sulawesi, reigning from 1653 to 1669.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-husayn"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sultan-husayn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sultan Husayn</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan Husayn, also known as Shah Sultan Husayn, was the Safavid ruler of Iran from 1694 to 1722.</sp