ultan of Sokoto is the ruler of the Sokoto Caliphate founded by Usman dan Fodio in 1804, styled Amir al-Mu'minin (Commander of the Faithful) and in Hausa Sarkin…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-said-khan"><span class="enc-name">Sultan Said Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan Said Khan was a Chagatai prince who founded the Yarkent Khanate in the Tarim Basin in 1514, taking Kashgar and Yarkand from the Dughlat lord Mirza Abu Bakr.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-shah-ibn-ridwan"><span class="enc-name">Sultan Shah ibn Ridwan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan Shah ibn Ridwan was the last Seljuk ruler of Aleppo, a son of Ridwan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-suriansyah"><span class="enc-name">Sultan Suriansyah</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan Suriansyah, born Raden Samudra, was the founder of the Banjar Sultanate in southern Borneo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-tangkal-alam-bagagar"><span class="enc-name">Sultan Tangkal Alam Bagagar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan Tangkal Alam Bagagar was the last ruler of the Pagaruyung kingdom in the Minangkabau highlands of Sumatra.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultan-thaha-saifuddin"><span class="enc-name">Sultan Thaha Saifuddin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sultan Thaha Saifuddin was ruler of the Jambi Sultanate in Sumatra from 1855.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-gowa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sultanate-of-gowa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sultanate of Gowa</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sultanate of Gowa was a Makas